A||||10||CUTTER||Neutral Droping bad?
Z||000000||CUTTER||08-26-99||10:52 PM||||I know Neutral droping is bad for the trans, But I couldnt help myself the first 2 months or so when I wanted to show off my blue 87GT, yes....its automatic...I cant spin the tires by slaming the gas or line locking it because they are too big and wide of tires, I neutral droped it probably almost 100 times mostly 3000-4000 rpm then throw her in drive. They say the trans is that Getrag or whatever....So far I have no trouble with the trans. How can I spin the tires without neutral droping it? I can get a chirp on a hill, to spin the tires by line locking it, do i need more horsepower? I want to keep my original tires too by the way.
Z||000001||Silver Bullet||08-26-99||11:19 PM||||wait until it rains :-)    As far as the nuetral slamming goes,  DON'T!!!! 
Z||000002||4Banger Bandit||08-26-99||11:22 PM||||Well, if it's an automatic, it's not a Getrag 5-sp.  ;o)  Try taking off on wet pavement, snow, ice, and grave.  Otherwise, do it the right way and start modding it.  Yes, it CAN be done.  
Z||000003||CUTTER||08-26-99||11:26 PM||||I know it is bad but is it that bad? Is it ok to do it in the rain? I dont really need to drop it in the rain because I can line lock it and spin um.<br>
Z||000004||lowCG||08-27-99||12:36 AM||||You either need to get an old muscle car with leaf springs,or maybe a torque converter with a higher stall speed,say around 2200 rpm.
Z||000005||BobC||08-27-99||05:12 AM||||When I was 21, I thought nuetral dropping was ok.  The rebuild was $400.  You have been very lucky, so far.<p>BobC
Z||000006||kornholio||08-27-99||10:22 AM||||Well, I did the same thing with my auto 86 SE until my reverse stopped working.  I had my transmission checked out and the mechanic said that there was nothing wrong it...just the trans fluid was dirty as shit.  I thought that I really messed up the transmission by neutral dropping it.  I've only done it like 4 or 5 times, but I've stopped because I'm afraid of the damage it may cause.<p><br>What's line locking?
Z||000007||lowCG||08-27-99||10:29 AM||||A line lock is an electrically controlled valve that goes to the front brakes,holding them on so that you can roast the rear tires.<br>Was sold as a "hill holder" through automotive aftermarket companies,but parts can be purchased commercially for cheaper.<br>Maybe just to get a pair of space saver spares would work too,heard they roast up real nice.
Z||000008||terryk||08-27-99||10:27 PM||||It will die eventually. The CV's will go too.<p>No trans guy can truthfully say it's "fine" without tearing it down.<p>
Z||000009||JimiZ||08-28-99||12:32 AM||||Things to think about: motor mounts, tranny mounts, cv shafts, trans front pump...<br>.<br>.<br>.<br>DON'T DO IT.<br>In highschool I had a 1971 Ford LTD 2DR, with a 351W in it.  60k miles.  Too heavy to burn em off, so I did ONE neutral drop and broke a motor mount, causing the engine to torque over, raise the fan up, bust the fan shroud, and slice a nice hole in the hood.  That sucked!  Try telling yer ole man that it was an accident, especially when he's a hotrodder like mine is...
Z||000010||theogre||08-28-99||09:03 PM||||You've beat the crap out of your car 100+- times????????? I'd about guarantee you've got problems with the tranny and other things. It just may be awhile befroe they show up..... probably at 2am in a really bad place.
